=== admit.mjs diff in completion commit ===
commit 71d64cfae4979457b901646480939ae8b93004a7
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 20:52:36 2026 +0000

    feat(bench): the environment factory synthesizes completion tasks from the bench's reference programs

    tools/synthesize-completion-tasks.mjs reads every parent under environments/,
    parses each reference/src/*.js file with a conservative brace/paren/string/
    comment/regex-literal/template-literal scanner (not a real parser) for
    top-level `function name(...) {` and `const name = (...) => {` declarations,
    and for each one long enough to matter (--min-lines, default 4; a file with
    more eligible functions than --max-functions-per-file, default 20,
    contributes none) writes environments-completion/<parent>--<function>/: the
    reference solution with that one function's body replaced by
    `throw new Error('not implemented')` (signature and leading comment/JSDoc
    kept), the parent's test/ and package.json unchanged, reference/ kept for
    admission, and a task.json carrying family/completion detail and checks
    stripped of any hidden-case check. Every stubbed file is checked with
    `node --check` and dropped if it fails to parse. --dry-run lists candidates
    without writing; --admit runs admit.mjs over the output, deletes what it
    rejects, and records why in REFUSED.json. Two files of one parent sharing a
    top-level function name are disambiguated by file stem, and the generated id
    tracks that disambiguation so admission's directory/id check does not reject
    the pair.

    admit.mjs's directory/id consistency check now strips a completion id's
    `--complete-` marker before comparing to the directory name, since only the
    id (not the directory) carries it; a no-op for every curated task's plain id.

    register-completion-environments.ts registers the admitted completion family
    under the same `bench` kind the curated 44 use, reading
    register-environments.ts's now-widened EnvironmentKindMap (two new optional
    detail fields, `family` and `completion`). It takes the completion directory
    as a validated Config field. overlays/with-completion.cordis.yml mounts it as
    a second producer beside the base composition; with-completion-openrouter
    mounts it beside the free open-weight route with-openrouter.cordis.yml
    names, since a driver takes exactly one config; registry-only-with-completion
    is the keyless variant the extended registrar e2e test boots.

    plans/completion-smoke-sonnet.json names six completion children across
    every tier; plans/completion-openrouter-free-t2.json names four tier-2
    children over three free OpenRouter models (12 cells). Neither plan has run.

    Committed environments-completion/ is the factory's own admitted output over
    the checked-in 44: 246 candidates from all 44 parents, 246 written (0 dropped
    for a parse failure), 246 admitted, 0 refused (REFUSED.json is []).

    (cherry picked from commit d800eba3f8c4f8a14a3f8317e4d791a9e57fe548)

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HEXjzxR7CyMizem5kFAB4C

